name","og:image","og:url","og:description","og:title","og:type","spotahome:ad","description","cityAvailabilitiesStatistics",[],"cityPricesStatistics",[],"cityTenantStatistics",["N",{"_219":220,"_221":222,"_223":224,"_211":225}],"cityUserInteractionStatistics",[203,204,205,206],["N",{"_207":217,"_209":218,"_211":212}],["N",{"_207":215,"_209":216,"_211":212}],["N",{"_207":213,"_209":214,"_211":212}],["N",{"_207":208,"_209":210,"_211":212}],"propertyType","studio","percentage",12.37,"__typename","UserInteractionStats","room_shared",55.92,"residence",2.92,"apartment",28.78,"ageDistribution",[251,252,253],"occupationType",[244,245],"nationality",[226,227,228,229],"TenantStats",["N",{"_223":241,"_209":242,"_232":243,"_211":234}],["N",{"_223":238,"_209":239,"_232":240,"_211":234}],["N",{"_223":235,"_209":236,"_232":237,"_211":234}],["N",{"_223":230,"_209":231,"_232":233,"_211":234}],"IT",8.748387096774193,"countryName","Italy","NationalityStats","DE",9.393548387096775,"Germany","FR",10.038709677419355,"France","PT",10.632258064516128,"Portugal",["N",{"_70":249,"_209":250,"_211":248}],["N",{"_70":246,"_209":247,"_211":248}],"professional",28.141459744168547,"CategoryCount","student",71.85854025583144,["N",{"_70":258,"_209":259,"_211":248}],["N",{"_70":256,"_209":257,"_211":248}],["N",{"_70":254,"_209":255,"_211":248}],"18-24",43.87096774193549,"41+",12.025806451612903,"25-40",44.10322580645161,"397301","947492","263039","basic",["N",{"_52":177,"_194":166,"_283":284,"_211":285}],"twitter",["N",{"_281":185,"_52":177,"_194":166,"_101":173,"_276":171,"_211":282}],"og",["N",{"_70":193,"_52":177,"_194":166,"_101":173,"_276":171,"_277":278,"_279":168,"_211":280}],["N",{"_52":271,"_272":40,"_273":274,"_211":275}],"Metadata","Find the best apartments for rent in Lisbon","subtitle","body","<section><p>Want to <a href=\"https://www.spotahome.com/s/lisbon\">live in Lisbon</a> and experience neighbourhood life? Accept the invitation and come and meet some neighbourhoods where you can find apartments to rent in Lisbon! Having everything at your fingertips! Living outside the city can have its advantages, but... waking up with the chickens, letting your alarm clock ring until you throw it against the wall or getting stressed by the traffic can give you the right to an ulcer. And picking up the car every time you need to go to the supermarket or want to get a coffee can be quite tiring. </p>\n\n<strong>Apartments in Lisbon</strong>\n<p>How about renting an apartment in Lisbon and saying goodbye to these day-to-day complications? If you make this choice and decide to settle down in one of the various neighbourhoods that the city has to offer, you will no longer have to worry about the car, because you will be able to do everything on foot! Or by bike! Or by public transport... In a city with over 500,000 inhabitants, in the neighbourhoods you can still greet someone you pass by with a \"Good morning, neighbour!\" Renting a flat in Lisbon brings the guarantee that you can go to the corner grocery store to buy whatever you need in 5 or 10 minutes. </p>\n\n<p>A trip to the theatre or a concert with only a few metro or bus stops between your home and the venue will be a reality if you choose to rent a one-room apartment in Lisbon. Alternative spaces and shops, restaurants from all over the world and for all occasions, gourmet shops, rental bikes and cycle paths will be within walking distance if you decide to rent a two-bedroom apartment in Lisbon! With so many apartments for rent in Lisbon just choose the experience you want to enjoy! In Castelo, you'll find stunning views; in Alfama, you're likely to hear someone singing fado if you leave the window open. And, when it's time for the popular saints, just go down to the street and taste a grilled sardine, accompanied by a beer! In Campo de Ourique or Alvalade, for example, you will find more tranquility and a shop for every need! It may be difficult to find cheap flats in Lisbon, but in this city, there is a bit of everything. </p>\n\n<strong>Which neighborhood to choose?</strong>\n<p>There are many flats for rent in Lisbon, both in the older districts and in the more modern ones. The choice will depend on your needs and, of course, your budget. Renting a two-room apartment in Lisbon for 400 euros? Very unlikely! To rent a three-bedroom in Lisbon for 500 euros? If you find one, bet on euromillions! If you want to rent a one-bedroom flat in Lisbon and you are willing to open the purse strings, you will find wonderful apartments, new or renovated, with wooden floors, huge windows where the unique Lisbon light comes in, in the most fashionable neighbourhoods of the city, like Chiado or Príncipe Real. </p>\n\n<p>If you need a bit more space, <a href=\"https://www.spotahome.com/s/lisbon/for-rent:apartments/bedrooms:2\">renting a two-room apartment in Lisbon</a> is also a good option and there are plenty to choose from, a bit all over the city. If you have to tighten your belt, you'll find flats at a slightly more affordable price in less central neighbourhoods, like Benfica, Ameixoeira, Belavista or Laranjeiras. <a href=\"https://www.spotahome.com/s/lisbon/for-rent:rooms\">Sharing a house</a> can also be a good option to be able to live in the more central neighbourhoods of Lisbon. Renting a 3 bedroom can be a great idea if you have a group of friends you want to live with until everyone goes their own way. In Lisbon, renting a 4-bedroom apartment? It is also possible! But, in this case, there are no trifles. </p></section>\n\n<section><h3>How much is an apartment in Lisbon?</h3>\n<p>You can expect to pay more in Lisbon than in other parts of the country. It's also important to note that prices vary depending on location, size and amenities. In general, you'll be paying more for an apartment in the city centre as opposed to suburban areas. If you're looking for something with a view of the castle or São Jorge Castle Tower then prepare yourself for some hefty price tags. </p>\n\n<p>The season also affects rental prices: it's possible to save up to 20% on your rent during off-peak months (November - April). </p></section>\n<section><h3>Which district in Lisbon is best connected to rent a flat? </h3>\n<p>As Lisbon is a big city and it is hard to say which district is best connected. However, Lisbon has a good metro system, which will take you anywhere in the city. The car sharing service allows residents to rent bikes from one station and drop them off at another station. </p>\n\n<p>The tram system covers parts of central Lisbon and its suburbs, such as Belém and Alcântara. It also connects these areas with other parts of the city including downtown Lisbon on lines 1 & 2 or Cais do Sodré on line 5 & 6. </p></section>\n<section><h3>How long does it take to find an apartment in Lisbon? </h3>\n<p>If you are looking for a particular type of flat, or a specific location, it may take longer to find the right place. If you do not have much time to spend on looking for a flat, we recommend booking the first available apartment that seems suitable. However, if you want to get the best deal and stay in the most popular areas of Lisbon then it is worth spending some time searching before making any decisions. </p>\n<p>The good news is that throughout January and February there are plenty of flats available at discounted prices as landlords try to rent out their properties quickly before they go on holiday so there should be no shortage of choices when hunting for accommodation in Lisbon during these months. </p></section>\n\n\n<section><h3>Where is a safe place to rent an apartment in Lisbon?</h3>\n<p>If you're keen to find the safest area in Lisbon, then the Bairro Alto, Cais do Sodre and Alfama are your best bets. These areas are centrally located (they're close to all the main shops and restaurants), but they're also away from the beach and river. The safest areas are usually those that aren't as popular with tourists (you'll find lots of locals here). So if you want an apartment or a <a href=\"https://www.spotahome.com/s/lisbon/for-rent:studios\">studio</a> that's safe from pickpockets or burglars, these are great places to start looking. </p>\n<p>If you're traveling with children then it's a good idea to take them out of the main tourist areas where there will be more people around - this can help keep them safe from muggers who prey on tourists who aren't paying attention or don't know their surroundings well enough yet. </p></section>\n<section><h3>Can you negotiate rent in Lisbon? </h3>\n<p>Rents in Lisbon are negotiable. The price you pay is not necessarily set in stone, and you’re not going to be penalized for trying to get a better deal. </p>\n<p>You can negotiate with the landlord directly. If you want to rent a flat from someone who lives in Lisbon, this is the most common option. Most landlords will be willing to negotiate with you over the rent price as well as other terms of your lease (e.g., length of lease). </p>\n<p>You can negotiate with an agent who represents the landlord if they have rented out their home or apartment on behalf of their client (or if they do so regularly). Many agents work on commission and will try to persuade you that they need more than one month’s deposit upfront due to high interest rates or other costs associated with renting out property—but it isn't true! Just ask around online or find an agent through word-of-mouth; there are plenty available! </p></section>\n<section><h3>Can a foreigner rent an apartment in Lisbon? </h3>\n<p>It’s not difficult to rent an apartment in Lisbon and it isn't difficult for foreigners to rent an apartment in Lisbon either. </p>\n<p>You can find many websites like Spotahome that will help you find an apartment in Lisbon even while you are living in another country. </p></section>\n<section><h3>How do I get a flat in Lisbon? </h3>\n<p>Renting a flat in Lisbon is easy and you can follow 3 different ways:\n<p>\n<p>If you prefer using an <strong>agent or realtor</strong> when finding your own place, there are plenty of companies that specialize in helping people find flats for rent in Lisbon. These companies usually charge a fee but will often be able to negotiate better deals than those found on their own.</p>\n<p>Many <strong>tourist offices</strong> offer assistance with finding apartments as well (though this service may come at an additional cost). </p>\n<p><strong>Try Spotahome!</strong>We have an extensive list of apartments that are available for rent. If you're looking for something specific, feel free to contact us and we'll see what we can do!\n</section>\n","SEOContent","imageUrl","siteName","Rent accommodation online in Lisbon","locale","OgMetadata","card","TwitterMetadata","indexable",true,"BasicMetadata","Information about our rentals in Lisbon","features",[290,291,292,293,294,295,296,297],"SeoSnippet",["N",{"_52":313,"_150":314,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":311,"_150":312,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":309,"_150":310,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":307,"_150":308,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":305,"_150":306,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":303,"_150":304,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":301,"_150":302,"_211":300}],["N",{"_52":298,"_150":299,"_211":300}],"☀️ With balcony/terrace","761 homes","Feature","💖 Ideal for couples","887 accommodations","🎓 Ideal for students","794 accommodations","🐶 Pets allowed","359 properties","💰 Deposit not required","167 rentals","✔️ Verified properties","968 homes","💵 Minimum monthly price","starting from 650 €","🏠 Nº of properties","1692 flats and apartments for rent","lat","38.722252","lng","-9.139337",{"_367":591,"_369":592,"_371":26,"_372":487,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_367":587,"_369":588,"_371":26,"_372":468,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_367":582,"_369":583,"_371":26,"_372":584,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_367":577,"_369":578,"_371":26,"_372":579,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_367":573,"_369":574,"_371":26,"_372":487,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_367":568,"_369":569,"_371":26,"_372":570,"_374":-5,"_375":-5},{"_